Not fixable, because that's the technology:
- One picture in means the back is a guess. That's why the pink fades round the sides and back. Feeding it more views (point 2 above) is the only fix.
- The splat stores colour only. TRELLIS writes the simplest kind of splat, so fur sheen won't shift as you move round it, and it looks flat.
- Only the outside exists. It can't know about the brain, the coil or the mini bear.
- The 1 m scale and sideways orientation are just TRELLIS's output conventions, not errors.